        "video_id": "z9fgKz1Drlc",
        "lecture": 6,
        "kind": "claim",
        "importance": 3,
        "text": "The playlist will be divided into three stages: stage one, stage two, and stage three.",
        "line_ids": [
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@146",
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@148",
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@151",
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@174",
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@176"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "z9fgKz1Drlc:p002",
        "video_id": "z9fgKz1Drlc",
        "lecture": 6,
        "kind": "claim",
        "importance": 3,
        "text": "Stage one focuses on the building blocks needed before training a large language model: data preprocessing and sampling, the attention mechanism, and the LLM architecture.",
        "line_ids": [
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@201",
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@204",
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@206",
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@209",
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@211",
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@214",
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@216",
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@220",
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@222",
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@224",
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@226"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "z9fgKz1Drlc:p003",
        "video_id": "z9fgKz1Drlc",
        "lecture": 6,
        "kind": "procedure",
        "importance": 2,
        "text": "In stage one, the course will cover how data is collected from different datasets, how it is processed, and how it is sampled.",
        "line_ids": [
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@229",
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@231",
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@234",
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@236"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "z9fgKz1Drlc:p004",
        "video_id": "z9fgKz1Drlc",
        "lecture": 6,
        "kind": "procedure",
        "importance": 3,
        "text": "In stage one, the course will build the attention mechanism from scratch in Python and explain key, query, value, attention scores, positional encoding, and vector embeddings.",
        "line_ids": [
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@236",
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@238",
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@240",
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@242",
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@245",
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@248",
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@250",
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@252"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "z9fgKz1Drlc:p005",
        "video_id": "z9fgKz1Drlc",
        "lecture": 6,
        "kind": "procedure",
        "importance": 3,
        "text": "In stage one, the course will cover the LLM architecture, including how to stack layers and where the attention head goes, to understand the basic mechanism behind a large language model.",
        "line_ids": [
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@252",
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@254",
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@257",
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@259",
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@261",
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@265",
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@268",
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@269",
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@272"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "z9fgKz1Drlc:p006",
        "video_id": "z9fgKz1Drlc",
        "lecture": 6,
        "kind": "definition",
        "importance": 3,
        "text": "A token can be thought of as a unit of a sentence.",
        "line_ids": [
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@276",
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@279",
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@281",
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@284",
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@286"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "z9fgKz1Drlc:p007",
        "video_id": "z9fgKz1Drlc",
        "lecture": 6,
        "kind": "procedure",
        "importance": 3,
        "text": "Tokenization breaks sentences down into individual tokens in a particular way.",
        "line_ids": [
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@276",
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@279",
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@281",
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@288",
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@290"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "z9fgKz1Drlc:p008",
        "video_id": "z9fgKz1Drlc",
        "lecture": 6,
        "kind": "definition",
        "importance": 3,
        "text": "Vector embedding transforms each word after tokenization into a very high-dimensional vector space so that semantic meaning between words is captured.",
        "line_ids": [
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@293",
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@296",
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@299",
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@301",
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@304"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "z9fgKz1Drlc:p009",
        "video_id": "z9fgKz1Drlc",
        "lecture": 6,
        "kind": "analogy",
        "importance": 2,
        "text": "In a vector embedding space, words with similar meanings should lie closer together, such as apple, banana, and orange; king, man, and woman; and football, golf, and tennis.",
        "line_ids": [
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@307",
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@310",
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@312",
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@314",
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@317",
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@318",
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@320",
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@322",
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@325",
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@327",
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@330",
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@332",
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@336",
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@338",
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@340"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "z9fgKz1Drlc:p010",
        "video_id": "z9fgKz1Drlc",
        "lecture": 6,
        "kind": "definition",
        "importance": 3,
        "text": "Positional encoding gives the model information about the order in which words appear in a sentence.",
        "line_ids": [
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@345",
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@347",
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@349",
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@352",
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@354"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "z9fgKz1Drlc:p011",
        "video_id": "z9fgKz1Drlc",
        "lecture": 6,
        "kind": "procedure",
        "importance": 2,
        "text": "The course will cover how to construct batches from a large dataset and feed those batches to the large language model.",
        "line_ids": [
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@355",
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@358",
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@361",
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@364",
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@366",
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@369",
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@371"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "z9fgKz1Drlc:p012",
        "video_id": "z9fgKz1Drlc",
        "lecture": 6,
        "kind": "definition",
        "importance": 3,
        "text": "The next-word prediction task gives a bunch of words and predicts the next word.",
        "line_ids": [
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@374",
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@376",
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@378"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "z9fgKz1Drlc:p013",
        "video_id": "z9fgKz1Drlc",
        "lecture": 6,
        "kind": "definition",
        "importance": 2,
        "text": "Context refers to how many words should be taken for training to predict the next output.",
        "line_ids": [
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@380",
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@382",
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@385"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "z9fgKz1Drlc:p014",
        "video_id": "z9fgKz1Drlc",
        "lecture": 6,
        "kind": "claim",
        "importance": 2,
        "text": "Batching the data in different sets makes computation much more efficient.",
        "line_ids": [
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@387",
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@391",
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@393"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "z9fgKz1Drlc:p015",
        "video_id": "z9fgKz1Drlc",
        "lecture": 6,
        "kind": "procedure",
        "importance": 2,
        "text": "Before pre-training, a data batching sequence is implemented before giving the dataset to the large language model.",
        "line_ids": [
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@396",
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@398",
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@401",
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@404"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "z9fgKz1Drlc:p016",
        "video_id": "z9fgKz1Drlc",
        "lecture": 6,
        "kind": "procedure",
        "importance": 3,
        "text": "The course will explain the parts of the Transformer attention mechanism, including multi-head attention, positional encoding, input embedding, and output embedding.",
        "line_ids": [
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@406",
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@408",
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@410",
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@412",
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@414",
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@416",
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@419",
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@421",
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@423",
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@425"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "z9fgKz1Drlc:p017",
        "video_id": "z9fgKz1Drlc",
        "lecture": 6,
        "kind": "claim",
        "importance": 3,
        "text": "Stage two is pre-training: after assembling the data and constructing the LLM architecture, code is written to train the model on the underlying dataset.",
        "line_ids": [
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@440",
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@443",
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@445",
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@447",
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@449",
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@451",
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@453",
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@455",
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@457",
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@460"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "z9fgKz1Drlc:p018",
        "video_id": "z9fgKz1Drlc",
        "lecture": 6,
        "kind": "definition",
        "importance": 3,
        "text": "Pre-training builds a foundational model on unlabeled data.",
        "line_ids": [
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@460",
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@463",
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@465",
          "z9fgKz1Drlc@467",
